-- R21 - Trend tag on every card and a trend cut in the weekly review; no gate change until 20 closed thematic cards
-- decide it (both Macro Takeaways digests).
-- Source: thread "Compare macro book with our trading rules", 16 Nov 2026 (Willer and Saunders, Trading Global Macro
-- Markets, against spec v19 and R01 to R20).
-- Proposed 16 Nov 2026 with dash.propose_rule; apply_after = Sun 22 Nov 2026 20:00 SGT unless "oppose R21".
-- Body, title, rationale and revert_if below are byte-identical to the DB row (body md5 7528b9f1e16b55d8f09d941a29617438);
-- the evidence is generalised (the DB copy carries realised R by bucket; this repo is public).
-- Code that goes with it: META key "trend" in _shared/parse.ts (stored once dash-ingest is re-pinned);
-- scripts/weekly_review/trend_cut.sql computes the bucket from dash.trend_state until then.
-- To put it in force before the Sunday window (one line in the Supabase SQL editor, project diiwqbxyhtgvozhncoef):
--   update dash.rules set status = 'in_force', decided_at = now(), apply_after = now() where rid = 'R21' and status = 'proposed';
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "Trend tag on every card and a trend cut in the weekly review; no gate change until 20 closed thematic cards decide it", "body": "TREND TAG AND TREND CUT (thread \"Compare macro book with our trading rules\", 16 Nov 2026). Willer and Saunders (Trading Global Macro Markets, Wiley 2026) find that momentum beats valuation at one-year and medium horizons in every asset class they test, that simple moving-average rules work, and that CTA and CFTC positioning is a trend signal rather than a fade except in equities. This book's first six weeks point the same way: thematic cards opened with the trend monitor's ensemble have hit more targets and fewer stops than those opened against it (counts in the evidence). R10's CARVER line already prints trend and carry on the card, but nothing records the alignment where the weekly review can cut by it. This rule adds the record, the cut and a decision point. It changes no gate, no fill, no exit and no size. Applies in both books.\n\n1. TAG. For every NEW card (thematic, tactical, hedge, convexity) whose proxy is, or tracks, a trend-monitor asset under R10 item 1's map, read once per run, in the same pass as the Carver block, `select asset_id, all_ens, state from dash.trend_state where run_date = (select max(run_date) from dash.trend_state)` (Supabase project diiwqbxyhtgvozhncoef; all_ens runs from -1 to +1 on the asset the monitor prices: a price for FX, equities and commodities, a YIELD for UST2Y, UST5Y, UST10Y, UST30Y, EUR10Y_AAA and JGB10Y). trend = direction x all_ens, where direction is +1 for a long and -1 for a short of the card's proxy, with the sign flipped once more for a bond-future proxy (ZT, ZF, ZN, ZB and other bond futures, where long the future is long bonds and the monitor's asset is the yield); a yield proxy (^IRX, ^FVX, ^TNX, ^TYX) takes no flip. Write it as the LAST key of META, after any R17 risk key: \"· trend <±x.xx>\" (two decimals, ASCII sign). A proxy with no monitor asset (a curve or spread, a ratio, ^VIX, HYG, EEM, a single stock) writes \"· trend -\". The tag is written once and never edited: a roll, a re-basing or a review leaves it.\nBuckets: WITH when trend is +0.33 or above, AGAINST when -0.33 or below, FLAT between; \"-\" is UNTAGGED.\n\n2. PRINT. On the NEW card and its TESTED line, directly after the CARVER line: \"TREND: <+x.xx with / -x.xx against / x.xx flat> (<state>, as of <run_date>)\". A THEMATIC card tagged AGAINST names it in its case against (\"against the trend: ensemble -0.78, STRONG_DOWN\") and its p reason must name what turns the trend (a dated catalyst, a positioning washout under R02, a policy change), never conviction alone. A tactical card is against the trend by construction and prints the tag without comment. Nothing is lowered, vetoed or re-gated.\n\n3. WEEKLY CUT. The weekly review adds one standing cut, closed cards by trend bucket x class (with / against / flat / untagged x thematic / tactical / hedge / convexity): n, wins, targets, stops, cum R as booked, cum R planned, average stated p. Until dash-ingest stores the trend key, the review computes each card's bucket from dash.trend_state at the latest run_date on or before the card's opened date, with the proxy map of R10 item 1 and the sign rule of item 1 above (the select is in the repo, scripts/weekly_review/trend_cut.sql); a card that carries the key uses the key.\n\n4. DECISION. When 20 closed THEMATIC cards carry a bucket other than untagged, or on 20 January 2027, whichever comes first, the weekly review reads the cut and proposes one of: (a) against-trend THEMATIC cards take a payoff haircut at test (c) in the form of R09, EV = p x r/r x 0.75 - (1 - p) x 1.25, if the against bucket averages below zero R while the with bucket averages above zero; (b) the tag stays as disclosure only, if the buckets do not differ by at least 0.3R on average; (c) a stricter rule, if the with bucket also loses. Until then no card is rejected, haircut or sized on this tag.\n\n5. FIRST RUN. Open and pending cards get no tag and no restatement; the SCORECARD is unchanged. The trade block's footer gains \"trend: <n> with · <m> against · <k> flat\" counting today's NEW cards.", "rationale": "Owner asked on 16 Nov 2026 for a comparison of Willer and Saunders' Trading Global Macro Markets with the Takeaways rules. The one place where the book and this book's own record agree is trend: the book's momentum and CTA-positioning results, and the split of our closed thematic cards by trend alignment at open. The spec has no trend input to the gate and the R10 Carver line is not stored, so the record cannot be cut by it without a hand query. A tag plus a cut costs one query already in the run and decides in a month whether a haircut is warranted; a haircut now would rest on 13 cards in one regime.", "evidence": "dash.trades (fable) to 16 Nov 2026: 23 closed cards map to a trend-monitor asset; 13 thematic (9 with the trend, 4 against) and 8 tactical (3 with, 5 against); 8 closed cards have no monitor asset. Thematic cards with the trend hit more targets and fewer stops than those against; tactical cards, against by construction, did fine. Six weeks, one regime. Realised R by bucket is in the database row only (this repo is public).", "revert_if": "Revert if a weekly review finds the tag mis-signed (a bond future or yield proxy read the wrong way) on 2 or more cards, or the dash.trend_state read failing on 3 or more runs in a week, or the step costing the 08:15 SGT landing on 2 or more days with no other failure to explain it. The decision of item 4 is taken once, at 20 closed thematic cards or on 20 January 2027.", "supersedes": null, "review_due": "2027-01-20", "source": "thread"}$j$::jsonb);
